window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b337-129ca8bea1556703.json"]={sha256:"129ca8bea1556703efb66f9bdc848a98c2f4ca66ef1096d5edb2f53e71613b6d",value:{"id":"b337","title":"高速鐵路軌道超高配置","titleEn":"Cant design for high-speed railway curves","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"高速鐵路軌道超高配置以「曲線超高不足與混合速度的取捨」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。超高把軌道平面旋轉以分擔曲線橫向作用，固定超高只能對特定速度平衡；快慢列車共享軌道時，需同時辨認超高不足與超高過剩。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops cant deficiency and mixed-speed trade-offs through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Cant rotates the track plane to balance part of the lateral action on a curve; fixed cant balances only a particular speed, so shared tracks require both deficiency and excess to be examined. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["速度分布","Speed distribution"],["曲率半徑","Curve radius"],["軌道超高","Track cant"],["不足與過剩","Deficiency and excess"],["順坡變化率","Ramp rates"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,2],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,2]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["速度分布","曲率半徑","軌道超高","不足與過剩","順坡變化率"],"labelsEn":["Speed distribution","Curve radius","Track cant","Deficiency and excess","Ramp rates"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2；y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm。只把 G 增加百分之十，y=137.36 mm。模型邊界：小傾角剛體平衡且使用指定有效軌距；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm；y=eq-actual=40 mm。只把 eq 增加百分之十，y=56.5 mm。模型邊界：平衡超高與實際超高採同一有效軌距；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2; y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm. Increasing only G with a ten-percent increase gives y=137.36 mm. Boundary: Small-angle rigid-body balance using the stated effective gauge; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm; y=eq-actual=40 mm. Increasing only eq with a ten-percent increase gives y=56.5 mm. Boundary: Equilibrium and actual cant use the same effective gauge; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b337-v16-s1","title":"平衡超高計算與超高不足辨認","titleEn":"Equilibrium cant calculation & Cant-deficiency calculation","description":"本階段聚焦「平衡超高計算」與「超高不足辨認」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equilibrium cant calculation\" and \"Cant-deficiency calculation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b337-v16-01","title":"平衡超高計算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equilibrium cant calculation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「平衡超高計算」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Equilibrium cant calculation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平衡超高由向心需求和重力分量匹配求得，所用軌距應明確定義。本模型把 G 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 137.36 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。小傾角剛體平衡且使用指定有效軌距。使用有效軌距與曲線半徑作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「平衡超高計算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Equilibrium cant matches centripetal demand with a gravity component, using an explicitly defined effective gauge. In this model, G is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 137.36 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Small-angle rigid-body balance using the stated effective gauge. Use effective gauge and curve radius as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Equilibrium cant calculation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2；y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2; y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「平衡超高計算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Equilibrium cant calculation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-01-k1","title":"平衡超高計算","titleEn":"Equilibrium cant calculation","text":"平衡超高由向心需求和重力分量匹配求得，所用軌距應明確定義。本模型把 G 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 137.36 mm。","textEn":"Equilibrium cant matches centripetal demand with a gravity component, using an explicitly defined effective gauge. In this model, G is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平衡超高計算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equilibrium cant calculation\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異","平衡超高由向心需求和重力分量匹配求得，所用軌距應明確定義。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error.","Equilibrium cant matches centripetal demand with a gravity component, using an explicitly defined effective gauge.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平衡超高由向心需求和重力分量匹配求得，所用軌距應明確定義。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Equilibrium cant matches centripetal demand with a gravity component, using an explicitly defined effective gauge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b337-v16-02","title":"平衡超高計算：定量估算","titleEn":"Equilibrium cant calculation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平衡超高計算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Equilibrium cant calculation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2；y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm。只把 G 增加百分之十，y=137.36 mm。模型邊界：小傾角剛體平衡且使用指定有效軌距；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2; y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm. Increasing only G with a ten-percent increase gives y=137.36 mm. Boundary: Small-angle rigid-body balance using the stated effective gauge; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以有效軌距與曲線半徑區分模型與觀察，先用超高尺、半徑與同步速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use effective gauge and curve radius to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2；y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm。只把 G 增加百分之十，y=137.36 mm。模型邊界：小傾角剛體平衡且使用指定有效軌距；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2; y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm. Increasing only G with a ten-percent increase gives y=137.36 mm. Boundary: Small-angle rigid-body balance using the stated effective gauge; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「平衡超高計算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equilibrium cant calculation\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2; y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2；y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: G=1.5 m, v=70 m/s, R=6000 m, g=9.81 m/s2; y=G*v**2/(g*R)*1000=124.873 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b337-v16-03","title":"平衡超高計算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equilibrium cant calculation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平衡超高計算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Equilibrium cant calculation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以有效軌距與曲線半徑區分模型與觀察，先用超高尺、半徑與同步速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平衡超高計算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use effective gauge and curve radius to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using cant level, radius and synchronized speed record, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Equilibrium cant calculation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「平衡超高計算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出小傾角剛體平衡且使用指定有效軌距如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異造成偏離的合成觀察，以有效軌距與曲線半徑說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Equilibrium cant calculation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Small-angle rigid-body balance using the stated effective gauge. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error. Explain which evidence in effective gauge and curve radius distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以有效軌距與曲線半徑區分模型與觀察，先用超高尺、半徑與同步速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平衡超高計算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use effective gauge and curve radius to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using cant level, radius and synchronized speed record, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Equilibrium cant calculation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「平衡超高計算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出小傾角剛體平衡且使用指定有效軌距如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異造成偏離的合成觀察，以有效軌距與曲線半徑說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Equilibrium cant calculation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Small-angle rigid-body balance using the stated effective gauge. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error. Explain which evidence in effective gauge and curve radius distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「平衡超高計算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equilibrium cant calculation\"?","options":["本單元以有效軌距與曲線半徑區分模型與觀察，先用超高尺、半徑與同步速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅"],"optionsEn":["Use effective gauge and curve radius to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以有效軌距與曲線半徑區分模型與觀察，先用超高尺、半徑與同步速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use effective gauge and curve radius to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b337-v16-04","title":"平衡超高計算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equilibrium cant calculation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平衡超高計算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Equilibrium cant calculation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異。這個失效與「平衡超高計算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查有效軌距與曲線半徑，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error. This failure and a measurement bias in Equilibrium cant calculation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check effective gauge and curve radius rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用有效軌距與曲線半徑作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異。這個失效與「平衡超高計算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查有效軌距與曲線半徑，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error. This failure and a measurement bias in Equilibrium cant calculation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check effective gauge and curve radius rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「平衡超高計算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equilibrium cant calculation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages."],"answer":1,"explanation":"代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b337-v16-05","title":"超高不足辨認：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cant-deficiency calculation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「超高不足辨認」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cant-deficiency calculation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平衡需求高於實際超高時留下向外未平衡作用。本模型把 eq 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 56.5 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。平衡超高與實際超高採同一有效軌距。使用速度分組後的平衡需求作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「超高不足辨認」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A balance requirement greater than installed cant leaves an outward unbalanced action. In this model, eq is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 56.5 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Equilibrium and actual cant use the same effective gauge. Use equilibrium demand grouped by speed as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cant-deficiency calculation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm；y=eq-actual=40 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm; y=eq-actual=40 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「超高不足辨認」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cant-deficiency calculation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-05-k1","title":"超高不足辨認","titleEn":"Cant-deficiency calculation","text":"平衡需求高於實際超高時留下向外未平衡作用。本模型把 eq 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 56.5 mm。","textEn":"A balance requirement greater than installed cant leaves an outward unbalanced action. In this model, eq is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超高不足辨認」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cant-deficiency calculation\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔","平衡需求高於實際超高時留下向外未平衡作用。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading.","A balance requirement greater than installed cant leaves an outward unbalanced action."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平衡需求高於實際超高時留下向外未平衡作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A balance requirement greater than installed cant leaves an outward unbalanced action. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b337-v16-06","title":"超高不足辨認：定量估算","titleEn":"Cant-deficiency calculation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超高不足辨認」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cant-deficiency calculation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm；y=eq-actual=40 mm。只把 eq 增加百分之十，y=56.5 mm。模型邊界：平衡超高與實際超高採同一有效軌距；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm; y=eq-actual=40 mm. Increasing only eq with a ten-percent increase gives y=56.5 mm. Boundary: Equilibrium and actual cant use the same effective gauge; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以速度分組後的平衡需求區分模型與觀察，先用同里程速度群與超高剖面建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use equilibrium demand grouped by speed to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm；y=eq-actual=40 mm。只把 eq 增加百分之十，y=56.5 mm。模型邊界：平衡超高與實際超高採同一有效軌距；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm; y=eq-actual=40 mm. Increasing only eq with a ten-percent increase gives y=56.5 mm. Boundary: Equilibrium and actual cant use the same effective gauge; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「超高不足辨認」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cant-deficiency calculation\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm；y=eq-actual=40 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm; y=eq-actual=40 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm；y=eq-actual=40 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: eq=165 mm, actual=125 mm; y=eq-actual=40 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b337-v16-07","title":"超高不足辨認：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cant-deficiency calculation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超高不足辨認」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cant-deficiency calculation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以速度分組後的平衡需求區分模型與觀察，先用同里程速度群與超高剖面建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高不足辨認」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use equilibrium demand grouped by speed to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using speed groups and cant profiles at matching chainage, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cant-deficiency calculation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「超高不足辨認」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出平衡超高與實際超高採同一有效軌距如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用造成偏離的合成觀察，以速度分組後的平衡需求說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cant-deficiency calculation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Equilibrium and actual cant use the same effective gauge. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages. Explain which evidence in equilibrium demand grouped by speed distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以速度分組後的平衡需求區分模型與觀察，先用同里程速度群與超高剖面建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高不足辨認」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use equilibrium demand grouped by speed to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using speed groups and cant profiles at matching chainage, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cant-deficiency calculation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「超高不足辨認」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出平衡超高與實際超高採同一有效軌距如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用造成偏離的合成觀察，以速度分組後的平衡需求說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cant-deficiency calculation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Equilibrium and actual cant use the same effective gauge. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages. Explain which evidence in equilibrium demand grouped by speed distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「超高不足辨認」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cant-deficiency calculation\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以速度分組後的平衡需求區分模型與觀察，先用同里程速度群與超高剖面建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use equilibrium demand grouped by speed to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以速度分組後的平衡需求區分模型與觀察，先用同里程速度群與超高剖面建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use equilibrium demand grouped by speed to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b337-v16-08","title":"超高不足辨認：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cant-deficiency calculation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超高不足辨認」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cant-deficiency calculation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用。這個失效與「超高不足辨認」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查速度分組後的平衡需求，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages. This failure and a measurement bias in Cant-deficiency calculation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check equilibrium demand grouped by speed rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用速度分組後的平衡需求作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用。這個失效與「超高不足辨認」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查速度分組後的平衡需求，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages. This failure and a measurement bias in Cant-deficiency calculation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check equilibrium demand grouped by speed rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「超高不足辨認」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cant-deficiency calculation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔","只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading.","Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b337-v16-s2","title":"超高過剩辨認與未平衡橫向加速","titleEn":"Cant-excess calculation & Unbalanced lateral acceleration","description":"本階段聚焦「超高過剩辨認」與「未平衡橫向加速」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cant-excess calculation\" and \"Unbalanced lateral acceleration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b337-v16-09","title":"超高過剩辨認：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cant-excess calculation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「超高過剩辨認」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cant-excess calculation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"慢車平衡需求較小，軌道傾斜可能使重力分量主導向內作用。本模型把 actual 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 92.5 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。低速平衡超高已獨立算得，不含車體懸吊。使用低速或停車時的傾斜量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「超高過剩辨認」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A slow train has a smaller balance requirement, allowing the inward gravity component to dominate. In this model, actual is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 92.5 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Low-speed equilibrium cant is independently calculated; suspension is excluded. Use cant during slow movement or a stop as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cant-excess calculation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm；y=actual-eq=80 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm; y=actual-eq=80 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「超高過剩辨認」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cant-excess calculation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-09-k1","title":"超高過剩辨認","titleEn":"Cant-excess calculation","text":"慢車平衡需求較小，軌道傾斜可能使重力分量主導向內作用。本模型把 actual 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 92.5 mm。","textEn":"A slow train has a smaller balance requirement, allowing the inward gravity component to dominate. In this model, actual is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超高過剩辨認」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cant-excess calculation\" is correct?","options":["慢車平衡需求較小，軌道傾斜可能使重力分量主導向內作用。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力"],"optionsEn":["A slow train has a smaller balance requirement, allowing the inward gravity component to dominate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"慢車平衡需求較小，軌道傾斜可能使重力分量主導向內作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A slow train has a smaller balance requirement, allowing the inward gravity component to dominate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b337-v16-10","title":"超高過剩辨認：定量估算","titleEn":"Cant-excess calculation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超高過剩辨認」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cant-excess calculation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm；y=actual-eq=80 mm。只把 actual 增加百分之十，y=92.5 mm。模型邊界：低速平衡超高已獨立算得，不含車體懸吊；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm; y=actual-eq=80 mm. Increasing only actual with a ten-percent increase gives y=92.5 mm. Boundary: Low-speed equilibrium cant is independently calculated; suspension is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以低速或停車時的傾斜量區分模型與觀察，先用低速通過紀錄與超高尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use cant during slow movement or a stop to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm；y=actual-eq=80 mm。只把 actual 增加百分之十，y=92.5 mm。模型邊界：低速平衡超高已獨立算得，不含車體懸吊；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm; y=actual-eq=80 mm. Increasing only actual with a ten-percent increase gives y=92.5 mm. Boundary: Low-speed equilibrium cant is independently calculated; suspension is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「超高過剩辨認」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cant-excess calculation\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm；y=actual-eq=80 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm; y=actual-eq=80 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm；y=actual-eq=80 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: actual=125 mm, eq=45 mm; y=actual-eq=80 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b337-v16-11","title":"超高過剩辨認：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cant-excess calculation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超高過剩辨認」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cant-excess calculation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以低速或停車時的傾斜量區分模型與觀察，先用低速通過紀錄與超高尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高過剩辨認」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use cant during slow movement or a stop to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-speed passage records and cant level, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cant-excess calculation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「超高過剩辨認」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出低速平衡超高已獨立算得，不含車體懸吊如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔造成偏離的合成觀察，以低速或停車時的傾斜量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cant-excess calculation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Low-speed equilibrium cant is independently calculated; suspension is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading. Explain which evidence in cant during slow movement or a stop distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以低速或停車時的傾斜量區分模型與觀察，先用低速通過紀錄與超高尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高過剩辨認」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use cant during slow movement or a stop to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-speed passage records and cant level, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cant-excess calculation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「超高過剩辨認」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出低速平衡超高已獨立算得，不含車體懸吊如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔造成偏離的合成觀察，以低速或停車時的傾斜量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cant-excess calculation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Low-speed equilibrium cant is independently calculated; suspension is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading. Explain which evidence in cant during slow movement or a stop distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「超高過剩辨認」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cant-excess calculation\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移","本單元以低速或停車時的傾斜量區分模型與觀察，先用低速通過紀錄與超高尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment.","Use cant during slow movement or a stop to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以低速或停車時的傾斜量區分模型與觀察，先用低速通過紀錄與超高尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use cant during slow movement or a stop to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b337-v16-12","title":"超高過剩辨認：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cant-excess calculation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超高過剩辨認」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cant-excess calculation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔。這個失效與「超高過剩辨認」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查低速或停車時的傾斜量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading. This failure and a measurement bias in Cant-excess calculation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check cant during slow movement or a stop rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用低速或停車時的傾斜量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔。這個失效與「超高過剩辨認」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查低速或停車時的傾斜量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading. This failure and a measurement bias in Cant-excess calculation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check cant during slow movement or a stop rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「超高過剩辨認」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cant-excess calculation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力"],"optionsEn":["Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b337-v16-13","title":"未平衡橫向加速：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Unbalanced lateral acceleration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「未平衡橫向加速」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Unbalanced lateral acceleration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"超高不足乘重力再除有效軌距可估未平衡橫向加速度。本模型把 g 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.28776 m/s2。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。小傾角近似且超高不足以公尺輸入。使用超高不足與橫向感測值作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「未平衡橫向加速」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cant deficiency times gravity divided by effective gauge estimates unbalanced lateral acceleration. In this model, g is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.28776 m/s2. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Small-angle approximation with cant deficiency in metres. Use cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unbalanced lateral acceleration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m；y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m; y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「未平衡橫向加速」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Unbalanced lateral acceleration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-13-k1","title":"未平衡橫向加速","titleEn":"Unbalanced lateral acceleration","text":"超高不足乘重力再除有效軌距可估未平衡橫向加速度。本模型把 g 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.28776 m/s2。","textEn":"Cant deficiency times gravity divided by effective gauge estimates unbalanced lateral acceleration. In this model, g is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「未平衡橫向加速」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Unbalanced lateral acceleration\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力","超高不足乘重力再除有效軌距可估未平衡橫向加速度。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement.","Cant deficiency times gravity divided by effective gauge estimates unbalanced lateral acceleration.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section."],"answer":1,"explanation":"超高不足乘重力再除有效軌距可估未平衡橫向加速度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cant deficiency times gravity divided by effective gauge estimates unbalanced lateral acceleration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b337-v16-14","title":"未平衡橫向加速：定量估算","titleEn":"Unbalanced lateral acceleration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「未平衡橫向加速」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Unbalanced lateral acceleration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m；y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2。只把 g 增加百分之十，y=0.28776 m/s2。模型邊界：小傾角近似且超高不足以公尺輸入；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m; y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2. Increasing only g with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.28776 m/s2. Boundary: Small-angle approximation with cant deficiency in metres; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以超高不足與橫向感測值區分模型與觀察，先用軌面座標橫向加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m；y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2。只把 g 增加百分之十，y=0.28776 m/s2。模型邊界：小傾角近似且超高不足以公尺輸入；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m; y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2. Increasing only g with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.28776 m/s2. Boundary: Small-angle approximation with cant deficiency in metres; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「未平衡橫向加速」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Unbalanced lateral acceleration\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m；y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m; y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m；y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, D=0.04 m, G=1.5 m; y=g*D/G=0.2616 m/s2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b337-v16-15","title":"未平衡橫向加速：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Unbalanced lateral acceleration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「未平衡橫向加速」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Unbalanced lateral acceleration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以超高不足與橫向感測值區分模型與觀察，先用軌面座標橫向加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「未平衡橫向加速」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using lateral accelerometer in track-plane coordinates, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Unbalanced lateral acceleration. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「未平衡橫向加速」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出小傾角近似且超高不足以公尺輸入如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力造成偏離的合成觀察，以超高不足與橫向感測值說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Unbalanced lateral acceleration, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Small-angle approximation with cant deficiency in metres. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement. Explain which evidence in cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以超高不足與橫向感測值區分模型與觀察，先用軌面座標橫向加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「未平衡橫向加速」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using lateral accelerometer in track-plane coordinates, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Unbalanced lateral acceleration. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「未平衡橫向加速」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出小傾角近似且超高不足以公尺輸入如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力造成偏離的合成觀察，以超高不足與橫向感測值說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Unbalanced lateral acceleration, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Small-angle approximation with cant deficiency in metres. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement. Explain which evidence in cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「未平衡橫向加速」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Unbalanced lateral acceleration\"?","options":["本單元以超高不足與橫向感測值區分模型與觀察，先用軌面座標橫向加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異"],"optionsEn":["Use cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以超高不足與橫向感測值區分模型與觀察，先用軌面座標橫向加速度計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b337-v16-16","title":"未平衡橫向加速：失效診斷","titleEn":"Unbalanced lateral acceleration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「未平衡橫向加速」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Unbalanced lateral acceleration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力。這個失效與「未平衡橫向加速」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查超高不足與橫向感測值，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement. This failure and a measurement bias in Unbalanced lateral acceleration can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用超高不足與橫向感測值作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力。這個失效與「未平衡橫向加速」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查超高不足與橫向感測值，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement. This failure and a measurement bias in Unbalanced lateral acceleration can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check cant deficiency and lateral sensor readings rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「未平衡橫向加速」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Unbalanced lateral acceleration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b337-v16-s3","title":"超高順坡梯度與超高變化時間率","titleEn":"Cant-ramp gradient & Temporal cant rate","description":"本階段聚焦「超高順坡梯度」與「超高變化時間率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cant-ramp gradient\" and \"Temporal cant rate\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b337-v16-17","title":"超高順坡梯度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cant-ramp gradient: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「超高順坡梯度」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cant-ramp gradient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"超高沿路線的變化形成扭轉，總超高相同時縮短順坡會加大梯度。本模型把 dh 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.733333 mm/m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。線性超高順坡，不含局部階躍。使用等距超高剖面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「超高順坡梯度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cant variation creates track twist; shortening a ramp increases its gradient even with unchanged total cant. In this model, dh is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.733333 mm/m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Linear cant ramp without local steps. Use equally spaced cant profile as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cant-ramp gradient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m；y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m; y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「超高順坡梯度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cant-ramp gradient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-17-k1","title":"超高順坡梯度","titleEn":"Cant-ramp gradient","text":"超高沿路線的變化形成扭轉，總超高相同時縮短順坡會加大梯度。本模型把 dh 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.733333 mm/m。","textEn":"Cant variation creates track twist; shortening a ramp increases its gradient even with unchanged total cant. In this model, dh is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超高順坡梯度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cant-ramp gradient\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動","超高沿路線的變化形成扭轉，總超高相同時縮短順坡會加大梯度。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.","Cant variation creates track twist; shortening a ramp increases its gradient even with unchanged total cant."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超高沿路線的變化形成扭轉，總超高相同時縮短順坡會加大梯度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cant variation creates track twist; shortening a ramp increases its gradient even with unchanged total cant. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b337-v16-18","title":"超高順坡梯度：定量估算","titleEn":"Cant-ramp gradient: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超高順坡梯度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cant-ramp gradient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m；y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m。只把 dh 增加百分之十，y=0.733333 mm/m。模型邊界：線性超高順坡，不含局部階躍；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m; y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m. Increasing only dh with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.733333 mm/m. Boundary: Linear cant ramp without local steps; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以等距超高剖面區分模型與觀察，先用等距雙軌水準量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use equally spaced cant profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m；y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m。只把 dh 增加百分之十，y=0.733333 mm/m。模型邊界：線性超高順坡，不含局部階躍；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m; y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m. Increasing only dh with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.733333 mm/m. Boundary: Linear cant ramp without local steps; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「超高順坡梯度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cant-ramp gradient\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m；y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m; y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m；y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m; y=dh/L=0.666667 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b337-v16-19","title":"超高順坡梯度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cant-ramp gradient: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超高順坡梯度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cant-ramp gradient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以等距超高剖面區分模型與觀察，先用等距雙軌水準量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高順坡梯度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use equally spaced cant profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using equally spaced level measurements of both rails, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cant-ramp gradient. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「超高順坡梯度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線性超高順坡，不含局部階躍如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段造成偏離的合成觀察，以等距超高剖面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cant-ramp gradient, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear cant ramp without local steps. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section. Explain which evidence in equally spaced cant profile distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以等距超高剖面區分模型與觀察，先用等距雙軌水準量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高順坡梯度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use equally spaced cant profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using equally spaced level measurements of both rails, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cant-ramp gradient. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「超高順坡梯度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線性超高順坡，不含局部階躍如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段造成偏離的合成觀察，以等距超高剖面說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cant-ramp gradient, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear cant ramp without local steps. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section. Explain which evidence in equally spaced cant profile distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「超高順坡梯度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cant-ramp gradient\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以等距超高剖面區分模型與觀察，先用等距雙軌水準量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use equally spaced cant profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以等距超高剖面區分模型與觀察，先用等距雙軌水準量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use equally spaced cant profile to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b337-v16-20","title":"超高順坡梯度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cant-ramp gradient: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超高順坡梯度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cant-ramp gradient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段。這個失效與「超高順坡梯度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查等距超高剖面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section. This failure and a measurement bias in Cant-ramp gradient can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check equally spaced cant profile rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用等距超高剖面作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段。這個失效與「超高順坡梯度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查等距超高剖面，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section. This failure and a measurement bias in Cant-ramp gradient can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check equally spaced cant profile rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「超高順坡梯度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cant-ramp gradient\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動","接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.","A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b337-v16-21","title":"超高變化時間率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Temporal cant rate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「超高變化時間率」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Temporal cant rate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"行車速度將空間超高梯度轉換成乘客經歷的時間變化率。本模型把 dh 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 44 mm/s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。固定速度通過線性超高順坡。使用車速與順坡里程同步資料作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「超高變化時間率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Train speed converts spatial cant gradient into the temporal rate experienced by occupants. In this model, dh is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 44 mm/s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Constant speed through a linear cant ramp. Use synchronized speed and ramp chainage as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Temporal cant rate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s；y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s; y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「超高變化時間率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Temporal cant rate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-21-k1","title":"超高變化時間率","titleEn":"Temporal cant rate","text":"行車速度將空間超高梯度轉換成乘客經歷的時間變化率。本模型把 dh 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 44 mm/s。","textEn":"Train speed converts spatial cant gradient into the temporal rate experienced by occupants. In this model, dh is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超高變化時間率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Temporal cant rate\" is correct?","options":["行車速度將空間超高梯度轉換成乘客經歷的時間變化率。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順"],"optionsEn":["Train speed converts spatial cant gradient into the temporal rate experienced by occupants.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join."],"answer":0,"explanation":"行車速度將空間超高梯度轉換成乘客經歷的時間變化率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Train speed converts spatial cant gradient into the temporal rate experienced by occupants. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b337-v16-22","title":"超高變化時間率：定量估算","titleEn":"Temporal cant rate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超高變化時間率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Temporal cant rate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s；y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s。只把 dh 增加百分之十，y=44 mm/s。模型邊界：固定速度通過線性超高順坡；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s; y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s. Increasing only dh with a ten-percent increase gives y=44 mm/s. Boundary: Constant speed through a linear cant ramp; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以車速與順坡里程同步資料區分模型與觀察，先用速度計與同步雙軌高程建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use synchronized speed and ramp chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s；y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s。只把 dh 增加百分之十，y=44 mm/s。模型邊界：固定速度通過線性超高順坡；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s; y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s. Increasing only dh with a ten-percent increase gives y=44 mm/s. Boundary: Constant speed through a linear cant ramp; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「超高變化時間率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Temporal cant rate\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s；y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s; y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s；y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: dh=120 mm, L=180 m, v=60 m/s; y=dh*v/L=40 mm/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b337-v16-23","title":"超高變化時間率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Temporal cant rate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超高變化時間率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Temporal cant rate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以車速與順坡里程同步資料區分模型與觀察，先用速度計與同步雙軌高程建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高變化時間率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use synchronized speed and ramp chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using speed sensor and synchronized rail levels, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Temporal cant rate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「超高變化時間率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定速度通過線性超高順坡如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動造成偏離的合成觀察，以車速與順坡里程同步資料說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Temporal cant rate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant speed through a linear cant ramp. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed. Explain which evidence in synchronized speed and ramp chainage distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以車速與順坡里程同步資料區分模型與觀察，先用速度計與同步雙軌高程建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高變化時間率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use synchronized speed and ramp chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using speed sensor and synchronized rail levels, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Temporal cant rate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「超高變化時間率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定速度通過線性超高順坡如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動造成偏離的合成觀察，以車速與順坡里程同步資料說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Temporal cant rate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Constant speed through a linear cant ramp. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed. Explain which evidence in synchronized speed and ramp chainage distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「超高變化時間率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Temporal cant rate\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔","本單元以車速與順坡里程同步資料區分模型與觀察，先用速度計與同步雙軌高程建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading.","Use synchronized speed and ramp chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以車速與順坡里程同步資料區分模型與觀察，先用速度計與同步雙軌高程建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use synchronized speed and ramp chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b337-v16-24","title":"超高變化時間率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Temporal cant rate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超高變化時間率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Temporal cant rate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動。這個失效與「超高變化時間率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查車速與順坡里程同步資料，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed. This failure and a measurement bias in Temporal cant rate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check synchronized speed and ramp chainage rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用車速與順坡里程同步資料作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動。這個失效與「超高變化時間率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查車速與順坡里程同步資料，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed. This failure and a measurement bias in Temporal cant rate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check synchronized speed and ramp chainage rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「超高變化時間率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Temporal cant rate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順"],"optionsEn":["A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join."],"answer":0,"explanation":"靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b337-v16-s4","title":"不足變化時間率與平衡速度反算","titleEn":"Deficiency change rate & Equilibrium-speed inversion","description":"本階段聚焦「不足變化時間率」與「平衡速度反算」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Deficiency change rate\" and \"Equilibrium-speed inversion\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b337-v16-25","title":"不足變化時間率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Deficiency change rate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「不足變化時間率」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deficiency change rate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"超高不足沿緩和段的變化反映曲率與超高兩個剖面是否協調。本模型把 dD 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 19.25 mm/s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。不足量沿里程線性改變且車速固定。使用曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「不足變化時間率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Deficiency change along a transition reflects coordination of curvature and cant profiles. In this model, dD is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 19.25 mm/s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Deficiency changes linearly with distance at fixed speed. Use curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Deficiency change rate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s；y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s; y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「不足變化時間率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Deficiency change rate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-25-k1","title":"不足變化時間率","titleEn":"Deficiency change rate","text":"超高不足沿緩和段的變化反映曲率與超高兩個剖面是否協調。本模型把 dD 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 19.25 mm/s。","textEn":"Deficiency change along a transition reflects coordination of curvature and cant profiles. In this model, dD is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「不足變化時間率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deficiency change rate\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順","超高不足沿緩和段的變化反映曲率與超高兩個剖面是否協調。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join.","Deficiency change along a transition reflects coordination of curvature and cant profiles.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"超高不足沿緩和段的變化反映曲率與超高兩個剖面是否協調。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Deficiency change along a transition reflects coordination of curvature and cant profiles. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b337-v16-26","title":"不足變化時間率：定量估算","titleEn":"Deficiency change rate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「不足變化時間率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deficiency change rate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s；y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s。只把 dD 增加百分之十，y=19.25 mm/s。模型邊界：不足量沿里程線性改變且車速固定；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s; y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s. Increasing only dD with a ten-percent increase gives y=19.25 mm/s. Boundary: Deficiency changes linearly with distance at fixed speed; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程區分模型與觀察，先用共里程曲率超高與速度資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s；y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s。只把 dD 增加百分之十，y=19.25 mm/s。模型邊界：不足量沿里程線性改變且車速固定；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s; y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s. Increasing only dD with a ten-percent increase gives y=19.25 mm/s. Boundary: Deficiency changes linearly with distance at fixed speed; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「不足變化時間率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deficiency change rate\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s；y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s; y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s；y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: dD=50 mm, L=200 m, v=70 m/s; y=dD*v/L=17.5 mm/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b337-v16-27","title":"不足變化時間率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Deficiency change rate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「不足變化時間率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deficiency change rate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程區分模型與觀察，先用共里程曲率超高與速度資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「不足變化時間率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using curvature, cant and speed on common chainage, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Deficiency change rate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「不足變化時間率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出不足量沿里程線性改變且車速固定如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順造成偏離的合成觀察，以曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Deficiency change rate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Deficiency changes linearly with distance at fixed speed. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join. Explain which evidence in curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程區分模型與觀察，先用共里程曲率超高與速度資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「不足變化時間率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using curvature, cant and speed on common chainage, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Deficiency change rate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「不足變化時間率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出不足量沿里程線性改變且車速固定如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順造成偏離的合成觀察，以曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Deficiency change rate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Deficiency changes linearly with distance at fixed speed. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join. Explain which evidence in curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「不足變化時間率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deficiency change rate\"?","options":["本單元以曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程區分模型與觀察，先用共里程曲率超高與速度資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力"],"optionsEn":["Use curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程區分模型與觀察，先用共里程曲率超高與速度資料建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b337-v16-28","title":"不足變化時間率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deficiency change rate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「不足變化時間率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deficiency change rate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順。這個失效與「不足變化時間率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join. This failure and a measurement bias in Deficiency change rate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順。這個失效與「不足變化時間率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查曲率剖面與超高剖面的共同里程，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join. This failure and a measurement bias in Deficiency change rate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check curvature and cant profiles on shared chainage rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「不足變化時間率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deficiency change rate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b337-v16-29","title":"平衡速度反算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equilibrium-speed inversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「平衡速度反算」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Equilibrium-speed inversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"反算速度含超高平方根，超高增加不會同比例提高平衡速度。本模型把 g 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 236.518 km/h。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。小傾角靜力平衡，不是允許營運速度。使用半徑與實測超高作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「平衡速度反算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Inverted speed contains the square root of cant, so cant increase does not raise equilibrium speed proportionally. In this model, g is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 236.518 km/h. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Small-angle static balance, not an allowed operating speed. Use radius and measured cant as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Equilibrium-speed inversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m；y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m; y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「平衡速度反算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Equilibrium-speed inversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-29-k1","title":"平衡速度反算","titleEn":"Equilibrium-speed inversion","text":"反算速度含超高平方根，超高增加不會同比例提高平衡速度。本模型把 g 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 236.518 km/h。","textEn":"Inverted speed contains the square root of cant, so cant increase does not raise equilibrium speed proportionally. In this model, g is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平衡速度反算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equilibrium-speed inversion\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值","反算速度含超高平方根，超高增加不會同比例提高平衡速度。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed.","Inverted speed contains the square root of cant, so cant increase does not raise equilibrium speed proportionally."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反算速度含超高平方根，超高增加不會同比例提高平衡速度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Inverted speed contains the square root of cant, so cant increase does not raise equilibrium speed proportionally. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b337-v16-30","title":"平衡速度反算：定量估算","titleEn":"Equilibrium-speed inversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平衡速度反算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Equilibrium-speed inversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m；y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h。只把 g 增加百分之十，y=236.518 km/h。模型邊界：小傾角靜力平衡，不是允許營運速度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m; y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h. Increasing only g with a ten-percent increase gives y=236.518 km/h. Boundary: Small-angle static balance, not an allowed operating speed; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以半徑與實測超高區分模型與觀察，先用半徑量測與實測超高建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use radius and measured cant to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m；y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h。只把 g 增加百分之十，y=236.518 km/h。模型邊界：小傾角靜力平衡，不是允許營運速度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m; y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h. Increasing only g with a ten-percent increase gives y=236.518 km/h. Boundary: Small-angle static balance, not an allowed operating speed; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「平衡速度反算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equilibrium-speed inversion\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m; y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m；y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: g=9.81 m/s2, R=5000 m, h=0.12 m, G=1.5 m; y=sqrt(g*R*h/G)*3.6=225.511 km/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b337-v16-31","title":"平衡速度反算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equilibrium-speed inversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平衡速度反算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Equilibrium-speed inversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以半徑與實測超高區分模型與觀察，先用半徑量測與實測超高建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平衡速度反算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use radius and measured cant to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using radius measurement and measured cant, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Equilibrium-speed inversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「平衡速度反算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出小傾角靜力平衡，不是允許營運速度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅造成偏離的合成觀察，以半徑與實測超高說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Equilibrium-speed inversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Small-angle static balance, not an allowed operating speed. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed. Explain which evidence in radius and measured cant distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以半徑與實測超高區分模型與觀察，先用半徑量測與實測超高建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平衡速度反算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use radius and measured cant to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using radius measurement and measured cant, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Equilibrium-speed inversion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「平衡速度反算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出小傾角靜力平衡，不是允許營運速度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅造成偏離的合成觀察，以半徑與實測超高說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Equilibrium-speed inversion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Small-angle static balance, not an allowed operating speed. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed. Explain which evidence in radius and measured cant distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「平衡速度反算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equilibrium-speed inversion\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以半徑與實測超高區分模型與觀察，先用半徑量測與實測超高建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use radius and measured cant to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以半徑與實測超高區分模型與觀察，先用半徑量測與實測超高建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use radius and measured cant to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b337-v16-32","title":"平衡速度反算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equilibrium-speed inversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平衡速度反算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Equilibrium-speed inversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅。這個失效與「平衡速度反算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查半徑與實測超高，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed. This failure and a measurement bias in Equilibrium-speed inversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check radius and measured cant rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用半徑與實測超高作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅。這個失效與「平衡速度反算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查半徑與實測超高，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed. This failure and a measurement bias in Equilibrium-speed inversion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check radius and measured cant rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「平衡速度反算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equilibrium-speed inversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值","線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed.","Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"線性外推速度會高估可平衡速度的增幅。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Linear extrapolation overstates the increase in balance speed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b337-v16-s5","title":"混合列車均方速度與超高量測不確定度","titleEn":"Mixed-traffic squared speed & Cant measurement uncertainty","description":"本階段聚焦「混合列車均方速度」與「超高量測不確定度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mixed-traffic squared speed\" and \"Cant measurement uncertainty\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b337-v16-33","title":"混合列車均方速度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mixed-traffic squared speed: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「混合列車均方速度」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mixed-traffic squared speed” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"若以平方速度需求加權，應先平方再平均，不能先取平均速度再平方。本模型把 p 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3778 m2/s2。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。兩群速度固定且權重相加為一。使用各速度群比例與平方速度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混合列車均方速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Weighting squared-speed demand requires squaring before averaging, not squaring the mean speed. In this model, p is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 3778 m2/s2. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Two fixed speed groups with weights summing to one. Use group proportions and squared speeds as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mixed-traffic squared speed” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s；y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s; y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「混合列車均方速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mixed-traffic squared speed”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-33-k1","title":"混合列車均方速度","titleEn":"Mixed-traffic squared speed","text":"若以平方速度需求加權，應先平方再平均，不能先取平均速度再平方。本模型把 p 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3778 m2/s2。","textEn":"Weighting squared-speed demand requires squaring before averaging, not squaring the mean speed. In this model, p is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混合列車均方速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mixed-traffic squared speed\" is correct?","options":["若以平方速度需求加權，應先平方再平均，不能先取平均速度再平方。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移"],"optionsEn":["Weighting squared-speed demand requires squaring before averaging, not squaring the mean speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若以平方速度需求加權，應先平方再平均，不能先取平均速度再平方。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Weighting squared-speed demand requires squaring before averaging, not squaring the mean speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b337-v16-34","title":"混合列車均方速度：定量估算","titleEn":"Mixed-traffic squared speed: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「混合列車均方速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mixed-traffic squared speed” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s；y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2。只把 p 增加百分之十，y=3778 m2/s2。模型邊界：兩群速度固定且權重相加為一；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s; y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2. Increasing only p with a ten-percent increase gives y=3778 m2/s2. Boundary: Two fixed speed groups with weights summing to one; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以各速度群比例與平方速度區分模型與觀察，先用車次計數與分群速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use group proportions and squared speeds to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s；y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2。只把 p 增加百分之十，y=3778 m2/s2。模型邊界：兩群速度固定且權重相加為一；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s; y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2. Increasing only p with a ten-percent increase gives y=3778 m2/s2. Boundary: Two fixed speed groups with weights summing to one; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混合列車均方速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mixed-traffic squared speed\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看安裝超高會漏掉高速通過的未平衡作用","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s；y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：感測器安裝傾角未校正會混入重力"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Installed cant alone misses the unbalanced action of fast passages.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s; y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uncorrected sensor roll mixes gravity into the measurement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s；y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: p=0.6 1, vf=70 m/s, vs=40 m/s; y=p*vf**2+(1-p)*vs**2=3580 m2/s2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b337-v16-35","title":"混合列車均方速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mixed-traffic squared speed: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「混合列車均方速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mixed-traffic squared speed” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以各速度群比例與平方速度區分模型與觀察，先用車次計數與分群速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「混合列車均方速度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use group proportions and squared speeds to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using train counts and grouped speed records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Mixed-traffic squared speed. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「混合列車均方速度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩群速度固定且權重相加為一如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值造成偏離的合成觀察，以各速度群比例與平方速度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Mixed-traffic squared speed, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Two fixed speed groups with weights summing to one. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed. Explain which evidence in group proportions and squared speeds distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以各速度群比例與平方速度區分模型與觀察，先用車次計數與分群速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「混合列車均方速度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use group proportions and squared speeds to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using train counts and grouped speed records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Mixed-traffic squared speed. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「混合列車均方速度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩群速度固定且權重相加為一如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值造成偏離的合成觀察，以各速度群比例與平方速度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Mixed-traffic squared speed, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Two fixed speed groups with weights summing to one. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed. Explain which evidence in group proportions and squared speeds distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混合列車均方速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mixed-traffic squared speed\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：靜態合格的順坡在更高速度可能造成更快滾動","本單元以各速度群比例與平方速度區分模型與觀察，先用車次計數與分群速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A statically acceptable ramp can produce faster roll at higher speed.","Use group proportions and squared speeds to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以各速度群比例與平方速度區分模型與觀察，先用車次計數與分群速度紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use group proportions and squared speeds to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b337-v16-36","title":"混合列車均方速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mixed-traffic squared speed: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「混合列車均方速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mixed-traffic squared speed” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值。這個失效與「混合列車均方速度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各速度群比例與平方速度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed. This failure and a measurement bias in Mixed-traffic squared speed can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check group proportions and squared speeds rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用各速度群比例與平方速度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值。這個失效與「混合列車均方速度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各速度群比例與平方速度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed. This failure and a measurement bias in Mixed-traffic squared speed can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check group proportions and squared speeds rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混合列車均方速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mixed-traffic squared speed\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移"],"optionsEn":["Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只使用平均速度會低估平方速度的平均值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using mean speed alone understates mean squared speed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b337-v16-37","title":"超高量測不確定度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cant measurement uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「超高量測不確定度」如何影響高速鐵路軌道超高配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cant measurement uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Cant design for high-speed railway curves”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"左右軌高程差的不確定度要保留兩側誤差與相關性。本模型把 ul 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.743303 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。左右軌誤差獨立，未納入共同零點偏差。使用左右軌交換測量的閉合差作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「超高量測不確定度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uncertainty in rail-level difference must retain both rail errors and their correlation. In this model, ul is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.743303 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Independent rail errors, excluding common zero bias. Use closure from swapped left-right measurements as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cant measurement uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm；y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm; y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「超高量測不確定度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cant measurement uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-37-k1","title":"超高量測不確定度","titleEn":"Cant measurement uncertainty","text":"左右軌高程差的不確定度要保留兩側誤差與相關性。本模型把 ul 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.743303 mm。","textEn":"Uncertainty in rail-level difference must retain both rail errors and their correlation. In this model, ul is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超高量測不確定度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cant measurement uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移","左右軌高程差的不確定度要保留兩側誤差與相關性。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment.","Uncertainty in rail-level difference must retain both rail errors and their correlation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"左右軌高程差的不確定度要保留兩側誤差與相關性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uncertainty in rail-level difference must retain both rail errors and their correlation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b337-v16-38","title":"超高量測不確定度：定量估算","titleEn":"Cant measurement uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超高量測不確定度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cant measurement uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm；y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm。只把 ul 增加百分之十，y=0.743303 mm。模型邊界：左右軌誤差獨立，未納入共同零點偏差；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm; y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm. Increasing only ul with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.743303 mm. Boundary: Independent rail errors, excluding common zero bias; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以左右軌交換測量的閉合差區分模型與觀察，先用左右交換的水準尺讀值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use closure from swapped left-right measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm；y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm。只把 ul 增加百分之十，y=0.743303 mm。模型邊界：左右軌誤差獨立，未納入共同零點偏差；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm; y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm. Increasing only ul with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.743303 mm. Boundary: Independent rail errors, excluding common zero bias; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「超高量測不確定度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cant measurement uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把較大超高視為所有列車都有利會忽略慢車負擔","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：接點突變會使實際扭轉集中於短區段","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm；y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Assuming larger cant benefits every train ignores slow-train loading.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A discontinuity concentrates actual twist into a short section.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm; y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm；y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: ul=0.5 mm, ur=0.5 mm; y=sqrt(ul**2+ur**2)=0.707107 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b337-v16-39","title":"超高量測不確定度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cant measurement uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超高量測不確定度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cant measurement uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以左右軌交換測量的閉合差區分模型與觀察，先用左右交換的水準尺讀值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高量測不確定度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use closure from swapped left-right measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using levelling readings with left-right reversal, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cant measurement uncertainty. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「超高量測不確定度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出左右軌誤差獨立，未納入共同零點偏差如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移造成偏離的合成觀察，以左右軌交換測量的閉合差說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cant measurement uncertainty, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Independent rail errors, excluding common zero bias. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment. Explain which evidence in closure from swapped left-right measurements distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以左右軌交換測量的閉合差區分模型與觀察，先用左右交換的水準尺讀值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「超高量測不確定度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use closure from swapped left-right measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using levelling readings with left-right reversal, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cant measurement uncertainty. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「超高量測不確定度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出左右軌誤差獨立，未納入共同零點偏差如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移造成偏離的合成觀察，以左右軌交換測量的閉合差說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cant measurement uncertainty, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Independent rail errors, excluding common zero bias. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment. Explain which evidence in closure from swapped left-right measurements distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「超高量測不確定度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cant measurement uncertainty\"?","options":["本單元以左右軌交換測量的閉合差區分模型與觀察，先用左右交換的水準尺讀值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：兩個剖面錯位時會在接點產生額外不平順"],"optionsEn":["Use closure from swapped left-right measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Misaligned profiles create an additional disturbance at the join."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以左右軌交換測量的閉合差區分模型與觀察，先用左右交換的水準尺讀值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use closure from swapped left-right measurements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b337-v16-40","title":"超高量測不確定度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cant measurement uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b337-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超高量測不確定度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cant measurement uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移。這個失效與「超高量測不確定度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查左右軌交換測量的閉合差，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment. This failure and a measurement bias in Cant measurement uncertainty can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check closure from swapped left-right measurements rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用左右軌交換測量的閉合差作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b337-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移。這個失效與「超高量測不確定度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查左右軌交換測量的閉合差，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment. This failure and a measurement bias in Cant measurement uncertainty can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check closure from swapped left-right measurements rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b337-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「超高量測不確定度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cant measurement uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：代入名義軌距卻沿用另一公式係數會產生系統差異"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mixing nominal gauge with a coefficient based on another gauge causes systematic error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"儀器零點漂移可能被誤認為整段超高偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Instrument zero drift can resemble a cant shift along the whole segment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b337-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b337-en.svg"}};
